  "scope": "Apply the PR #443 multi-agent review findings to the provider-neutral structured-decision pipeline without changing OpenAI request bytes or the ten decision policies.",
  "fixes": [
    "Ollama decision requests send the trusted context as a user message after the system instructions (previously two system messages, which some chat templates render as an empty prompt).",
    "Anthropic decision streams skip leading thinking/redacted_thinking blocks with sequential indexes; thinking after text, a second text block and open blocks at message_delta fail closed.",
    "Anthropic decisions request max_tokens 4096, matching the existing Anthropic dialogue request, because current Claude models think by default and thinking counts against max_tokens.",
    "Provider selection in the serializer and client factory is explicit; an unknown provider throws instead of falling through to Ollama/Anthropic shapes.",
    "The OpenAI client takes the descriptor like the Anthropic and Ollama clients; descriptor serialization/lifecycle members are internal; lifecycle flags have no defaults; the shared 128-token bound is one constant.",
    "An unsupported response media type keeps its own fixed message instead of the generic invalid-stream message.",
    "The ten decision task controllers log the faulted exception type name instead of discarding it.",
    "Comment accuracy fixes, the composition smoke pass message, and 50 per-kind test files renamed away from deleted OpenAiCharacter* type names."
  ],
